  "name": "CHRONIC EOSINOPHILIC LEUKAEMIA (CEL) PANEL",
  "code": "2302",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1277\" data-end=\"1396\">\n<p data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1396\"><strong data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1315\">If FIP1L1-PDGFRA fusion detected</strong>: Suggestive of CEL with tyrosine kinase fusion, likely to respond to imatinib.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1397\" data-end=\"1522\">\n<p data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1522\"><strong data-start=\"1399\" data-end=\"1443\">If PDGFRB or FGFR1 rearrangement present</strong>: Indicates CEL or myeloid neoplasm with eosinophilia and gene rearrangement.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1523\" data-end=\"1641\">\n<p data-start=\"1525\" data-end=\"1641\"><strong data-start=\"1525\" data-end=\"1554\">If JAK2/KIT/ABL1 detected</strong>: May suggest alternative myeloproliferative neoplasm (MPN) or systemic mastocytosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1642\" data-end=\"1762\">\n<p data-start=\"1644\" data-end=\"1762\"><strong data-start=\"1644\" data-end=\"1675\">If all markers are negative</strong>: Consider idiopathic hypereosinophilic syndrome (HES) or further NGS-based assessment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
